{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '465,520p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md\"","aggregated_output":"\nThis does not require a semantic change to B0 through B5. B3 already makes\nloading and continuation state explicit, and B4 carries park and resume as\ndata transitions. The VM accepts loaded images only as values in its state and\nnever invokes a loader; absence is a park plus a request emission. B6 is the\nadditive phase for request and response streams, the\nlinked dimension, `:call-hash`, cycle handling, and failure policy.\n\nCompletion requires hash-address loading, cycle-safe manifests, explicit\nauthority, gap and timeout outcomes, malformed or missing-address diagnostics,\nand differential tests showing named and linked images agree where the name\nenvironment is fixed. It must not alter the projection fingerprint. It does\nnot establish global distribution or any property of the Unison runtime,\nwhich is UNVERIFIED here.\n\n### 7.3 Lossless source view non-goal\n\nThe VM does not build a second lossless record DAG. Named datoms remain the\nlossless source, and lexical positions, binder diagnostics, and provenance are\nderived into the executable image as needed. A separate inverse view would\nrequire its own design and is outside B0 through B6.\n\n## 8. Risks and owner decisions\n\nRisks include divergence from front-end tail flags, exact scalar spelling,\nnamed-VM environment leakage, malformed bound operands, source-map loss, and\nUCF's deferred transport contract.\n\nOwner decisions, ranked by B0 blocking impact:\n\n1. B0 blocker: the exact result, error, closure, continuation, and stream\n   normalizer.\n2. B1 decision: approve the executable scalar domain and\n   `:yin.debruijn.code/*` descriptor.\n3. B5 decision: fix the named VM environment leak or formally exclude it from\n   cross-program park/resume parity fixtures.\n4. B6 blocker: define what `:call-hash H` identifies, including whether the\n   image descriptor or contract stamp is inside H.\n5. B6 decision: authority ledger and trust/provenance, SCC identity, and\n   request-stream retry, timeout, and permanent-absence policy. The linker\n   boundary and local/remote transport are already fixed as `dao.stream`.\n6. B3 exit decision: the benchmark reports numbers only. Making the frame VM\n   default is an owner decision; retiring the semantic VM requires its own\n   design because it has existing consumers.\n7. Later decision: whether source-to-projection lineage is persisted.\n\n## 9. What this design must not change\n\nThe AST schema, AST walker, named emitter, named linearizer, semantic VM,\nexisting `:yin.code/*` dimension, `dao.stream` protocols, lease layer, waitset,\nnamed storage, projection algorithm, and projection fingerprint remain\nunchanged. The executable encoding and VM are additional artifacts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
