{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'optional lossless|encode-db|decode-db|inverse|lossless source|image may differ|lossless image|B0 blocker|owner decision|B6' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md; awk 'length(\"'$0)>80 {print NR \":\" length($0) \":\" $0}'\"' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md; rg -n '—|\\\\|' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md || true\"","aggregated_output":"8:lossless source view is built. The projection remains a separate identity and\n59:decoding and debugging; the executable image is not an inverse encoding.\n122:discovery are outside B0 through B6. Existing `:yin.code/*` semantics are\n384:hash linking before B6, and any change to the projection or its fingerprint.\n474:never invokes a loader; absence is a park plus a request emission. B6 is the\n488:lossless source, and lexical positions, binder diagnostics, and provenance are\n489:derived into the executable image as needed. A separate inverse view would\n490:require its own design and is outside B0 through B6.\n492:## 8. Risks and owner decisions\n523:- B6 request schema, contract stamps, SCC manifest mechanics, and the exact\n527:No owner decision blocks B0. B0 starts with D1 and the frozen parity corpus.\n70:    | Requirement              | Mechanism                                  |\n72:    | I: share executable code | Canonical image hash, verified loading,    |\n73:    | over dao.stream           | stream request and response (§2, §7.2).   |\n74:    | Everything is a stream   | Effects, transfer, linking and failure    |\n75:    |                          | are stream outcomes (§4, §7.2).           |\n76:    | No hidden global state   | VM state, free-env and registries are     |\n77:    |                          | explicit values (§4).                     |\n78:    | No implicit control flow | Steps classify explicit data; missing     |\n79:    |                          | code parks and emits a request (§7.2).    |\n80:    | No callbacks             | No loader or callback is invoked; events  |\n81:    |                          | cross stream boundaries (§7.2).           |\n82:    | No shared mutable state  | Frames, stores and continuations are      |\n83:    |                          | persistent transition data (§4).          |\n84:    | No layer collapse       | Projection, lowering, VM and linker are   |\n85:    |                          | separate interpreters (§1, §7.2).         |\n86:    | No assumed graphs       | Image refs and body ranges are validated  |\n87:    |                          | before execution (§3).                    |\n88:    | Derive, do not persist   | Named datoms stay authoritative; lexical  |\n89:    |                          | positions are derived (§1).               |\n90:    | Interpretation semantics| Named and de Bruijn VMs are compared by  |\n91:    |                          | the explicit normalizer (§1, B0).         |\n92:    | Host boundaries         | Cross-host common domain is tested;       |\n93:    |                          | unsupported classes refuse (§2, B1).      |\n94:    | Strained: frame env     | Frames require a lift for completion and  |\n95:    |                          | exported continuations (§4, B4).         |\n96:    | Strained: image state   | Loaded images are explicit values; the   |\n97:    |                          | linker must supply missing-code events.   |\n98:    | Strained: diagnostics   | Binder names and provenance are side data |\n99:    |                          | and never executable identity (§2, §3).   |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
